  "step_2": "The individual considers the outcomes of the two lotteries, specifically noting that Lottery A involves twice the loss of Lottery B (-6000 vs. -3000). The individual also observes that the probabilities of loss are very low for both lotteries. The justification for the choice seems to rest on the magnitude of the loss, emphasizing that the loss in A is double that in B, while acknowledging that the probabilities of loss are small. There is no mention of probability weighting, expected value, or systematic comparison of all outcome pairs. The focus is on the relative size of the worst outcome and its improbability.",
